## MCP Server Tools (Primary -- Use These First)

### Core Tools (read-only, no permission needed)

| MCP Tool | Args | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| `get_all_jobs` | (none) | List root-level jobs with name, URL, status |
| `get_job` | `job_path` | Job details by slash-separated path (e.g. `CI-Jobs/e2e_ui_test_pipeline`) |
| `get_build` | `job_path`, `build_number?` | Build info; omit build_number for last build |
| `get_build_log` | `job_path`, `build_number?`, `start?`, `max_lines?` | Console output as text (default 500 lines) |
| `get_build_status` | `build_url` | Quick status check from full build URL |
| `get_pipeline_stages` | `job_path`, `build_number?` | Pipeline stage names, statuses, durations (wfapi) |

### Analysis Tools (read-only, no permission needed)

| MCP Tool | Args | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| `analyze_pipeline` | `build_url`, `max_depth?`, `console_lines?` | Root cause failure analysis with fix recommendations |
| `get_downstream_tree` | `build_url`, `max_depth?`, `output_format?` | Downstream job tree (tree/markdown/json) |
| `get_test_results` | `job_path`, `build_number?`, `mode?` | Test results: summary, full, or failures |
| `analyze_test_results` | `job_path`, `build_number?`, `failures_only?`, `output_format?` | Component/squad test breakdown |

### State-Changing Tool (REQUIRES PERMISSION)

| MCP Tool | Args | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| `trigger_build` | `job_path`, `parameters?` | Trigger a build with optional params. **MUST ask user first.** |

## Job Path Format

Use slash-separated paths for `job_path` arguments. The MCP handles conversion to Jenkins API format automatically.

```
"CI-Jobs"                              → Lists jobs in CI-Jobs folder
"CI-Jobs/e2e_ui_test_pipeline"         → Specific pipeline in nested folder
"CI-Jobs/CLC/some-job"                 → Deeply nested job
```

For `build_url` arguments, pass the full Jenkins URL:
```
https://jenkins-csb-rhacm-tests.dno.corp.redhat.com/job/CI-Jobs/job/e2e_ui_test_pipeline/123/
```

## When to Use MCP vs CLI

| Scenario | Use |
|----------|-----|
| Get job info, build details, stages, status | MCP `get_job`, `get_build`, `get_pipeline_stages` |
| Failure analysis | MCP `analyze_pipeline` |
| Downstream tree | MCP `get_downstream_tree` |
| Test results | MCP `get_test_results`, `analyze_test_results` |
| Console log | MCP `get_build_log` |
| Monitor running build (polling) | CLI `jenkins-run monitor <URL>` |
| Map JIRA params to Jenkins | CLI `jenkins-run params <URL>` |
| Trigger with --dry-run preview | CLI `jenkins-run trigger <URL> --dry-run` |

## CLI Fallback Setup

```bash
source /Users/ashafi/Documents/work/ai/tools/integrations/jenkins/jenkins-env.sh
```

| CLI Command | Equivalent MCP Tool |
|-------------|-------------------|
| `jenkins-run analyzer --url <URL> --no-verify-ssl` | `analyze_pipeline(build_url=<URL>)` |
| `jenkins-run tree --url <URL> --no-verify-ssl` | `get_downstream_tree(build_url=<URL>)` |
| `jenkins-run results <URL>` | `get_test_results(job_path, build_number)` |
